Building the Debian package
===========================

The Cargo workspace depends on the sibling repository
`../netlink-packet-umbrawg` through a path dependency. A binary build must
therefore run from a combined tree:

    <root>/umbrawg-tools/
    <root>/netlink-packet-umbrawg/

scripts/package/make-dist.sh creates such a tree and
scripts/package/build-deb.sh runs dpkg-buildpackage inside it.

Crates from crates.io are fetched during the build unless they have already
been vendored. For an offline or reproducible build, run `cargo vendor` in
the umbrawg-tools directory, add the generated source replacement to
.cargo/config.toml, and build with `DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS="nocheck"` if the test
suite is not required.

A source upload (-S) needs the netlink crate vendored or packaged separately;
this package currently targets binary builds (-b).
